{
  "case_id": "2011-11-45",
  "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Harvey A. Schwartz",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question in this case is whether it is fairly discernible from the Civil Service Reform Act that Congress revoked the district court jurisdiction to declare acts of Congress unconstitutional in actions brought by Federal employees. The answer is no, for several reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- suppose an employee is fired and he has a variety of different kinds of claims, constitutional and statutory. What would you think happens then? Does he bring the constitutional claims in one court but the statutory claims in another court -- excuse me -- in the -- in the commission?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: In -- in those cases, did the -- did the plaintiffs also have nonconstitutional claims which they were pursuing in the Federal Circuit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: -- but there's unconstitutional executive action. There's an as- applied claim. Let's say that a plaintiff says that the registration requirement is unconstitutional as applied to me, not to other people, but to me because I'm a conscientious objector or I have religious objections to military action that the United States is taking at this particular time. And then there's this -- there's a claim that this statute is unconstitutional on its face. Now, where do you -- which of those can the Merit Systems Protection Review Board decide? Just the first category?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Now, in your original briefs, Mr. Schwartz, you suggested that if the MSPB can't hear a claim, neither can the Federal Circuit. And as I understood the Government's brief, the Government comes back and said that's not the case. Even when the MSPB can't hear a claim, the Federal Circuit could hear it. Now, then there's a question of, if there's a necessity for a record, how does the record get developed? But do you now concede that the Federal Circuit could hear the claim as a matter -- you know, on the -- at the -- at the first level?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schwartz",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SCHWARTZ: That's a system that -- that could come up. It's not the system of the Civil Service Reform Act in -- because --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can you go back and tell me when the government changed its position? It was my understanding that up until, well, certainly this case was litigated, the government was taking the position MSPB has no jurisdiction to pass on the constitutionality of a statute. When did the government back away from that position? When did it say, no, we were wrong; they do have jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, even if the MSPB lacks the authority to strike down a Federal statute, I still think it might be able to adjudicate the claim of the employee, the second employee, who brings it as an as-applied challenge because the Court would -- I'm sorry; not the Court -- the MSPB could"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Mr. Feigin, they might well be the same claim, but if the MSPB can decide the one and cannot decide the other, that's a relevant distinction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When we -- just let me rephrase that. If -- if this Court adopts a certain interpretation based on the principle of constitutional avoidance, do you think the Court is rewriting the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute does not, as we explain in our brief, draw any distinction between the types of arguments that would be made in seeking to set aside an unlawful discharge"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the MSPB does not have that authority. However --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the MSPB has a special rule -- I believe it's 5 C.S.R. 1201.61; it's cited in our brief -- where even if the MSPB decided not to accept evidence for some reason, a description of the evidence would go in the record and, therefore, be available for the Federal Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In any event, the Court has recognized that in Thunder Basin, for example, where review in the first instance was in the court of appeals, that the court of appeals had adequate authority to give meaningful judicial review to a constitutional claim that an agency, in that case the Mine Commission, by hypothesis could not decide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Harvey A. Schwartz",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to do is to see whether it's fairly discernible from the Civil Service Reform Act as it was written by Congress, not as it's twisted or amended or bent to fit these claims in it, but whether the Civil Service Reform Act as written by Congress revokes that background Federal court jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-45",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0a2ac402f7b9b4a1802f640beca1e5c571a6b66b6da61346fc43bbb4943115f3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0a2ac402f7b9-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: The case is submitted."
    },
